# Akeyless Provider

The Akeyless provider provides resources to interact with Akeyless services.

## Example Usage

{{tffile "examples/main.tf"}}

## Authentication with environment variables

Every login method can be configured without a login block. Leave the provider block empty and set environment variables instead:

```terraform
provider "akeyless" {}
```

Choose the login method with the `access_type` argument or the `AKEYLESS_ACCESS_TYPE` environment variable, and set the variables that method needs:

| `access_type` | Required | Optional |
|---|---|---|
| `auto` (default) | see below | |
| `api_key` (or `access_key`) | `AKEYLESS_ACCESS_ID`, `AKEYLESS_ACCESS_KEY` | |
| `password` | `AKEYLESS_EMAIL`, `AKEYLESS_PASSWORD` | |
| `aws_iam` | `AKEYLESS_ACCESS_ID` | |
| `gcp` | `AKEYLESS_ACCESS_ID` | `AKEYLESS_GCP_AUDIENCE` |
| `azure_ad` | `AKEYLESS_ACCESS_ID` | |
| `jwt` | `AKEYLESS_ACCESS_ID`, and `AKEYLESS_AUTH_JWT` or `AKEYLESS_AUTH_JWT_FILE` | |
| `universal_identity` | `AKEYLESS_AUTH_UID` | `AKEYLESS_ACCESS_ID` |
| `cert` | `AKEYLESS_ACCESS_ID`, `AKEYLESS_AUTH_CERT`, `AKEYLESS_AUTH_KEY` | |
| `token` | `AKEYLESS_AUTH_TOKEN` | |

With `auto`, the provider tries, in order:

1. API key, when `AKEYLESS_ACCESS_ID` and `AKEYLESS_ACCESS_KEY` are set.
2. JWT, when `AKEYLESS_ACCESS_ID` and `AKEYLESS_AUTH_JWT` or `AKEYLESS_AUTH_JWT_FILE` are set.

`AKEYLESS_AUTH_JWT_FILE` names a file that holds the JWT, for example a Kubernetes projected service account token or a CI-issued OIDC token written to disk. Set only one of `AKEYLESS_AUTH_JWT` and `AKEYLESS_AUTH_JWT_FILE`.

An unsupported `access_type`, or missing variables for the selected method, is an error.

A login block in the provider configuration always takes precedence over `AKEYLESS_ACCESS_TYPE`. Arguments left out of a login block are read from the same environment variables, for example:

```terraform
provider "akeyless" {
  jwt_login {} # access_id from AKEYLESS_ACCESS_ID, jwt from AKEYLESS_AUTH_JWT
}
```

Set the gateway address with `AKEYLESS_GATEWAY`.

This is useful in CI systems that issue OIDC tokens, such as GitHub Actions or env0: export the token as `AKEYLESS_AUTH_JWT` and use the same configuration locally with a different login method.

